{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.archimedean_agreement_of_sameElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.archimedean_agreement_of_sameElement","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L183-L192","doc":"**Archimedean agreement — DERIVED, not axiomatized.** Given the algebraic\nsame-element identification, the archimedean realization `ρ_∞` (evaluation at\n`u_0 = √q_0`) of the Habiro trace equals the GB mass, because `ρ_∞` is a ring\nhom that commutes with the finite decomposition. Axiomatizes strictly less\nthan `HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement`: one *algebraic*\npolynomial identity, versus a transcendental real equality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBSameElement.same_element","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBSameElement.same_element","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L181-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBSameElement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBSameElement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L180-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBSameElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBSameElement","kind":"class","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L172-L181","doc":"**The single open algebraic input (§3b-cond class, no instance).** The Habiro\ncyclotomic construction and the GB residue-spectral construction yield the\n*same* element of `Ẑ[q]` — an equality of polynomial representatives, hence in\nthe Habiro ring. This is the GS-filtration ↔ cyclotomic-projection\nidentification (`prop:graded-markov-trace-from-gs-filtration` +\n`prop:residue-at-root`), deferred to the algebraic-substrate layer; it is\n**algebraic**, not an analytic continuation. No instance is provided (the\nhonest open state). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.gb_mass_is_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.gb_mass_is_eval","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L169-L169","doc":"GB internal consistency: the mass is the archimedean eval of the GB\npolynomial representative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.gb_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.gb_mass","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L166-L166","doc":"The GB mass value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.gb_trace_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.gb_trace_poly","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L164-L164","doc":"GB residue-sum polynomial representative in `Ẑ[q]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.habiro_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.habiro_trace","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L162-L162","doc":"Habiro cyclotomic polynomial `Σ a_m (u;u)_m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.q_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.q_0","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L160-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L159-L159","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroGBData","kind":"structure","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L154-L170","doc":"Bundled data for the §3b-cond agreement: the two polynomial representatives\nand the GB mass, with the GB side's own internal consistency (`gb_mass` is\nthe archimedean evaluation of the GB polynomial representative — true by the\nGB residue-sum construction being a Habiro element; *not* the\ncross-identity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.trivialZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.trivialZero","kind":"instance","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L129-L139","doc":"Trivial-zero skeleton: every numerical field is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.q_0_proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.q_0_proton","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L115-L118","doc":"Substrate parameter `q_0 = 1.10997...` (proton pin) used throughout the\nphysical-prediction chapters.  Real-valued; `Real.sqrt q_0`\ngives `u_0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.archimedean_agreement","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L97-L97","doc":"**Analytic identity (substrate axiom).**\n\nThe archimedean realization of the Habiro polynomial trace at\n`u_0 = q_0^{1/2}` agrees with the GB residue-sum mass.\n\nThis is the formal counterpart to the cross-pipeline witness\n`markov-pipeline-cross-validation.witness.json`, which checks\nthis equality numerically at relative tolerance `1e-9` and\nconsistently achieves rel_diff ≤ machine epsilon on every\navailable atom.  The Lean proof is open at the level of\n`gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean`'s `noncomputable opaque`\ndeclarations. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:gs-archimedean-agreement-trace","label":"conj:gs-archimedean-agreement-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gs-archimedean-agreement-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.gb_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.gb_mass","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The GB residue-sum mass value in `ℝ` (matches\n`GBResidueSpectralSum.mass`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.habiro_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.habiro_trace","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The Habiro polynomial trace in `ℤ[u]` (matches\n`HabiroCompletion.trace`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.q_0_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.q_0_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Non-negativity of the substrate parameter (so `q_0^{1/2}` is real). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.q_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.q_0","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Archimedean evaluation point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidueSumEquivalence","kind":"class","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.lean#L48-L98","doc":"**Equivalence of the two Markov-trace constructions.**\n\nA `HabiroResidueSumEquivalence` instance records, for one fixed\nbraid word `T_w` and one fixed substrate parameter `q_0 ∈ ℝ`,\nthe agreement of the polynomial-ring evaluation of the Habiro\ntrace polynomial at `u_0 = q_0^{1/2}` with the GB residue-sum\nmass — both viewed in `ℝ` via the archimedean realization\n`ρ_∞ : Ẑ[q] → ℝ`.\n\nFields:\n* `q_0`              — the substrate parameter (archimedean evaluation point).\n* `habiro_trace`     — the Habiro polynomial trace, in `ℤ[u]`.\n* `gb_mass`          — the GB residue-sum mass value, in `ℝ`.\n* `archimedean_agreement` — the substantive axiom:\n  `eval (q_0^{1/2}) (map (Int.castRingHom ℝ) habiro_trace) = gb_mass`.\n  This is an **analytic identity**, currently axiomatized; a\n  Lean proof would require formalising the identification of\n  `Σ_m a_m(u_0) · (u_0;u_0)_m` with the residue spectral sum\n  `descended + Σ_ℓ Res_{q→ζ_ℓ}(Φ_q · tr_{M,ℓ})`.\n\nNo physical-atom instance is provided here (the honest open state);\nthe numerical cross-pipeline agreement recorded in\n`markov-pipeline-cross-validation.witness.json` is a computation, not\na Lean premise.\n\nRef: [habiro2004], [jones1987]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:habiro-residue-sum-equivalence","label":"prop:habiro-residue-sum-equivalence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-residue-sum-equivalence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}